shiryo-kit
==========

This product includes software derived from consulting-pptx-skill
(https://github.com/carnot-tech/consulting-pptx-skill, commit bc9a587f, 2026-10-14),
distributed under the MIT License. shiryo-kit is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or an official version of that project or its authors. Trademarks of the original
authors are not used in the name of this product.

Derived files (modified unless noted):
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/html_to_pptx.py   speaker notes, neutral document properties, dependency messages, bullet text box widened by the hanging indent (add_text)
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/html_dump.mjs     keeps the author's spaces between Japanese characters, never draws aside.notes, text export, effective CSS zoom applied to font sizes, spacing and borders
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/lib_cdp.mjs       Chrome/Edge/Chromium discovery (macOS/Windows/Linux), SHIRYO_CHROME_WAIT_MS, error messages
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/check_deck.py     no hard-coded tool name, parts path, notes excluded, rule-document references removed (not changed since; the relaxed title rules live in check.py)
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/new_deck.py       parts path, empty <aside class="notes"> per slide, split_css finds the first <style> after stripping HTML comments, upstream copyright line in the generated deck's header comment
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/pptx_open.py      unchanged
  skill/shiryo-kit/scripts/data/banned_phrases.txt   partly from the upstream AI-smell word list
  skill/shiryo-kit/assets/parts/freeform_parts_16x9.html        default back-cover credit line removed
  skill/shiryo-kit/assets/parts/freeform_parts_more_16x9.html   unchanged except header comment
  skill/shiryo-kit/assets/kata/*/sample.html (seminar, advisory, proposal, report)
                                             sample decks assembled by new_deck.py from the two parts files above:
                                             their CSS and slide markup come from the upstream templates; text is fictional
  tests/unit/fixtures/sample_deck.html       test deck assembled the same way

Decks that new_deck.py writes for you also contain CSS and markup from the two parts files.
Each generated deck carries a header comment with the copyright line above; keep it, together with
this NOTICE, when you redistribute the HTML. (The slides themselves do not show any credit line.)

